# Safari MP3 playback (do not “improve”)

Desktop was always fine. Phones play the element itself. A Web Audio graph on a phone wedges every browser, including Chrome, until the phone restarts.

All playback goes through `playSong` / `unlockAudio` in `client/src/lib/audioCache.ts`. MP3 prep is `prepareMp3` in `server/media.ts`.

## Required behavior

- Desktop: play immediately at full volume. Do not attach `createMediaElementSource`. Do not mute or hold.
- Mobile only (`isMobilePlayback`): do not create an `AudioContext` or call `createMediaElementSource`. One `play()` inside the tap, unmuted, at the listener's volume. Do not mute, and do not call `play()` again from `pause` or a premature `ended`.
- Keep Xing on VBR (Echoes). Strip Xing only on CBR.
- Stream the file URL. Do not prefetch bytes, Cache API audio, or blob/`createObjectURL` playback.

## Never do again (each of these failed or cut the first note)

- Play after a timeout (Safari drops the gesture)
- Prefetch the first ~1.5MB (Safari caches a stub)
- Blob URL or `spodazo-audio-*` Cache playback
- Strip Xing from VBR
- Seek to `START_OFFSET` after `play()`
- Close or recreate the AudioContext when the next song starts (it stays silent until the next tap)
- Call `createMediaElementSource` or `createScriptProcessor` on a phone
- Release MediaElementSource on the same element for auto-advance (cannot reattach; next song silent)
- Force 48 kHz `AudioContext` or unlock a different element
- Rely on `audio.volume = 0` alone on iOS
- Wait for `playing` + `currentTime` + a long fade (cuts music on desktop too)

If a change needs both a playback tweak and a new approach, keep this contract and add a failing test first.
